# High-Level Architecture Docs

When a change introduces or materially changes architectural details of significant value, document them in the relevant Docusaurus section.

Keep this documentation high level. Focus on how the system is composed, which parts are involved, and how they fit together. Do not turn it into low-level implementation notes or code commentary unless the user asks for that depth.

Examples of details worth documenting:
- How encryption works in `gitdb`, including which keys are used and how the pieces fit together
- How the timeline works in the webapp
- How the SQL database works in the iOS app, including the underlying git repo DB, how delta changes are written in transactions, and how pubsub broadcasts changes
